## 6. RESTRICTIONS & COMPATIBILITY:
restrictions:
  max_io_current: "300mA"
  total_current_limit: "300mA"
  warnings[9]:
    - "DVP12SS211S has only 4 transistor outputs (Y0-Y3) at 0.3A each with PNP sourcing — the output current of 0.3A per point is significantly lower than the 0.5A typical of larger PLCs; for loads exceeding 0.3A (solenoid valves above 7W at 24VDC, contactors, high-current LEDs) install an external relay or solid-state relay on each output; the total DO current should not exceed 0.8A on the common DO_S terminal; built-in short-circuit protection will limit current but repeated short-circuits damage the transistor junction over time"
    - "The 4 PTO channels (Y0-Y3) are limited to 10kHz maximum — this means a maximum stepping rate of 10,000 pulses/second per axis; for a typical stepper motor with 200 steps/rev at 10kHz, the maximum speed is 3,000 RPM (50 RPS × 60); for high-speed CNC applications requiring >10kHz pulse rates use the DVPPT01-SL positioning module which supports up to 200kHz; the PTO and HSC share the same high-speed input/output resources — running PTO and HSC on the same pin simultaneously is not possible"
    - "PWM DA output (PWM-to-analog conversion) is available ONLY on Y0 and Y1 on the DVP12SS211S — Y2 and Y3 do NOT support PWM DA output; the PWM output must be filtered with an external RC circuit (minimum 100Ω + 100µF electrolytic) to convert the PWM signal to a DC voltage (0-10VDC); the ripple voltage at 10kHz with a 100Ω+100µF filter is approximately 50mV; for applications requiring clean analog output without ripple install a DVPAE04-SL analog output module instead of using the PWM DA method"
    - "The RS-232 COM1 port (RJ25 6P4C front connector) is NOT ISOLATED from the internal CPU logic — connecting the RS-232 port to a PC or HMI with a different earth potential will cause a ground loop that may corrupt communications or damage the CPU UART; always use a USB-to-RS232 isolator or optically isolated RS-232 cable when connecting to a laptop or PC that does not share the same panel earth; the RS-485 COM2 port is also not isolated and the same precaution applies for remote panels with separate earthing"
    - "The RS-485 COM2 port supports a maximum cable length of 50m at 115200 bps — at lower baud rates (9600 bps) the cable can be extended to approximately 1,000m; when using 50m+ cables at high baud rates, install a 120Ω termination resistor between the + and - terminals at the far end of the RS-485 bus; the DVP12SS211S provides internal RS-485 bus biasing but the termination resistor is NOT built-in; without termination at high baud rates, signal reflections will cause Modbus CRC errors and communication timeouts"
    - "The maximum expansion I/O capacity of 480 points requires multiple right-side slim extension modules — the DVP12SS211S CPU provides internal 5V bus power to expansion modules from its internal regulated supply, but this supply is limited; always calculate the total current consumption of all connected expansion modules from Appendix D of the official Delta DVP operation manual before finalizing module selection; exceeding the CPU's expansion bus current capacity causes random I/O module faults, module initialization failures, and CPU reset"
    - "The program capacity is 8k steps ONLY — this is the smallest program memory in the DVP slim series; for applications requiring more than 8k steps (approximately 500-800 ladder rungs with basic logic), upgrade to DVP28SS211S (8k steps, same but 14DI+14DO) or DVP12SA211S (4k steps but with built-in analog) or DVP20SX211T (16k steps with analog and 200kHz HSC); 8k steps is sufficient for typical single-machine sequential control but will be insufficient for complex state-machine or motion applications"
    - "The left-side special module slot (DVPEN01-SL for Ethernet, DVPDNET-SL for DeviceNet, etc.) supports ONLY ONE module — if both Ethernet and PROFIBUS connectivity are required simultaneously, this is NOT possible with a single DVP12SS211S; plan the communications architecture before selecting the DVP-S model; the DVPEN01-SL Ethernet module adds Modbus TCP client/server capability but does NOT add EtherNet/IP support (only Delta proprietary Modbus TCP over Ethernet); for EtherNet/IP use the DVP-SE series PLC which has built-in EtherNet/IP"
    - "DVP12SS211S has NO built-in RTC (Real-Time Clock) by default — clock functions (time-of-day scheduling, timestamped data logging) are not available without an external RTC module; the internal M1511-M1517 RTC registers may be present in firmware but are battery-backed only if a backup battery accessory is installed; without a battery, the clock resets to 00:00:00 on every power cycle; always verify the availability of the RTC function for the specific firmware version using WPLSoft's PLC information dialog before relying on clock-based logic in the application"
compatibility:
  sw: "WPLSoft V2.30+ (primary; Windows 7/8/10/11); ISPSoft V3.00+ (advanced IEC editor); COMMGR V1.10+ (communication manager); DCISoft (device monitoring); Delta DIAScreen for HMI configuration"
  languages: "Instruction List (IL);Ladder Diagram (LD);Sequential Function Chart (SFC) via STL"
  frameworks: "Modbus-ASCII;Modbus-RTU;Delta-Host-Link;PLC-Link;DeviceNet-slave-via-DVPDNET-SL;PROFIBUS-DP-slave-via-DVPPFB-SL;CANopen-master-via-DVPCOPM-SL;Ethernet-Modbus-TCP-via-DVPEN01-SL"
  certifications: "CE;cULus-UL508;cCSAus;RCM;EAC-GOST;TUV;SEMI-F47;RoHS"

